# For <gsi dir>/system-hide (see ramdisk/init): OneUI (MysticGSI) apps that
# run on this board although disabled, since OneUI enables them again at boot.
# Samsung Device Health Manager: a NullPointerException at start, about 15
# crashes per boot, each one followed by a bug report (dumpstate)
system/priv-app/SamsungDeviceHealthManagerService
# com.qti.qcc: waits for a Qualcomm HAL (IQccsyshal) this vendor doesn't have,
# so it never finishes starting: an ANR, a stack dump and a restart every minute
system/system_ext/app/QCC
# Persistent too, so disabling them (to save RAM) left them running, about
# 100 MB each: Samsung's diagnostics agent and the VEX framework (camera
# effects). Not IMS (com.sec.imsservice): Samsung's Telecom in system_server
# fails to bind without it, and system_server crash-loops at every boot
system/priv-app/DiagMonAgent95
system/priv-app/vexfwk_service
